    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/godunov_norm_D2_dirichlet_bc: a minimal consuming model binding NX=NY=4 at the import edge. The COMPOUND match sqrt((D(u,x))^2 + (D(u,y))^2) fires (priority 10) through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint before any inner D could be lowered, lowering to the rule's makearray (doubly-interior Godunov-norm aggregate over [2,3]x[2,3]; four mirror-ghost edge strips at i=1,i=NX,j=1,j=NY; four corners) with the imported interior stencil inlined, the Dirichlet faces carrying the free names gL, gR, gB, gT and dx, dy, all metaparameters folded, zero apply_expression_template nodes, zero unlowered rewrite-target ops. gL, gB homogeneous (0); gR, gT nonzero (1) so the inhomogeneous face terms appear. x0=y0=0, dx=1/4, dy=1/4 spelled with the literal 4 (the import edge binds NX/NY; grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm contract). The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST across bindings.",
